-- `List.render()` drawing each member through its own view is not built: `core/List/List.js` belongs to the data backbone build. `view(list)` already does it.
+- **`List.View = DefaultView`** (2026-11-02, chat-model step 4): `list.render()` and `view(list)` both draw through it now. Its `reconcile()` keeps one view per member, keyed by the member itself (a `Map`), so an `add`/`remove`/`move`/`order`/`clear` only touches the rows that changed — a new member gets a fresh row, a gone one's row leaves, the rest just move in the DOM if their position shifted. A Ref member (`core/Item/Ref.js`) is drawn by `RefView`, never a nested `DefaultView` of its own near-empty data.
 
